Upstream repository: https://github.com/vprover/vampire
Reference commit: b75190a4b7946c325263b079ac8a67d2ea1c3e01

Vampire.txt preserves the complete original licence, copyright and disclaimer.
Vampire.AUTHORS and Vampire.THANKS preserve the original author list and
acknowledgements. Fang contributors are listed separately in CONTRIBUTORS.md.

Source files consulted (Fang paths on the left, upstream paths after the colon):

- src/syntax.rs: Kernel/Term.hpp and Kernel/Clause.hpp. Fang uses owned finite
  term trees and numeric identifiers, without the upstream allocation model.
- src/unify.rs: Kernel/RobSubstitution.cpp:237-356 and Kernel/RobSubstitution.hpp.
  Reference for worklist unification, occurs checking and rollback. Fang uses
  recursive expansion and occurs checks, owned bindings and transactional copies.
- src/search.rs: Inferences/BinaryResolution.cpp:250-264,
  Inferences/Factoring.cpp:45-104, Saturation/SaturationAlgorithm.cpp:1262-1345
  and Kernel/InferenceStore.cpp:883-953. Reference for resolution, factoring
  and search. Fang uses a bounded FIFO loop and its own certificate serializer.

The parser, predicate index, independent Lean checker and TSTP exporter are
new implementations. Kernel/InferenceStore.cpp:661-740 was read as context
for proof output; its printer implementation was not copied.

Fang is independent and is not endorsed by the Vampire authors. New Fang
contributions use the root LICENSE. Source and binary distributions must
retain the applicable copyright, licence conditions and disclaimers, with
separate notices for any bundled third-party components.
